1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The Organic Moderator Reactor Experiment, an important part of the Atomic Energy Commission's research program aimed at achieving economical nuclear power, has been developed at the National Reactor Testing Station.

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:56,000
This experiment, commonly referred to as OMBRE, is being conducted by Atomics International to study the use of organic substances as a coolant, heat transfer, and neutral moderator.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:11,379
The OMRE facility consists of three main sections.

4
00:01:11,379 --> 00:01:17,019
The operation building, which houses the control room and product preparation zones, the heat

5
00:01:17,019 --> 00:01:27,500
exchanger and air blowers, and the reactor core, installed underground beneath the building.

6
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:32,239
Systems related to the use of organic coolants have been studied in the Laboratories of Atomics

7
00:01:32,239 --> 00:01:35,680
International in California.

8
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:40,680
The stability of various organic compounds was determined through studies conducted in

9
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:44,280
a thermal loop and under different thermal cycles.

10
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:49,780
The thermal loop was built to circulate hydrocarbon mixtures through the material testing reactor

11
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:55,620
at the National Reactor Testing Station under conditions similar to those expected during

12
00:01:55,620 --> 00:02:03,520
the operations of OMBRE. A thermal circuit was used to determine heat transfer characteristics

13
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:11,580
and deposits produced by the organic fluids. For the design and operations of OMBRE, as

14
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:17,920
well as its purification system, the decomposition rates of various organic coolants were determined,

15
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,600
and methods of purifying them were studied.

16
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:27,820
As a result, a compound from the polyphenol group

17
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:30,580
was selected as the hydrocarbon for OMBRE.

18
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:38,340
The OMBRE cooling system contains over 19,000 liters

19
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:42,780
of a polyphenol mixture, whose characteristics, once melted,

20
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:44,960
are similar to those of water.

21
00:02:44,960 --> 00:03:07,400
The coolant enters the fuel element zone from the bottom of the vessel that houses the core, rises between the fuel plates to remove heat, descends between the fuel elements and control rods, and finally rises between the thermal shield and the vessel wall to a tank located above the core.

22
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:15,300
The organic compound is pumped from the reactor to the heat exchanger, which operates in connection

23
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:21,040
with air blowers, where the heat is dissipated and the coolant returns to the reactor, forming

24
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:25,300
the primary circuit.

25
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:30,400
The primary cooling system is fed by transferring molten hydrocarbon to the drainage tank.

26
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:38,780
It is filled via the expansion tank using the feed pump.

27
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:43,900
The purification system removes decomposition products from the hydrocarbon.

28
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:50,840
The facility receives the coolant from the heat transfer circuit.

29
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:56,319
The purified substance is recovered and sent to the feed tank from which the coolant can

30
00:03:56,319 --> 00:04:09,419
be pumped back into the system.

31
00:04:09,419 --> 00:04:13,979
The control of the organic substance during its circulation through the reactor system

32
00:04:13,979 --> 00:04:16,980
is carried out from the operations building.

33
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:23,719
This building is divided into two main parts by a protective wall.

34
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:28,480
In the control room, the control console, instrumentation equipment, and electrical

35
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:35,020
switchboard are located.

36
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:40,100
Adjacent to the control room is the organic compound melting station, nitrogen distributors,

37
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:47,280
and general storage area.

38
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:52,640
On the other side of the concrete protective wall is the recovery zone, which houses pumps

39
00:04:52,639 --> 00:04:58,639
for the organic coolant, the purification system, and associated equipment.

40
00:05:03,639 --> 00:05:11,639
The temperature of the organic compound in the low-pressure OMBR system ranges from 260 to 380 °C.

41
00:05:15,639 --> 00:05:21,639
Behind the recovery zone is the heat exchanger, which operates in connection with an air blower.

42
00:05:22,639 --> 00:05:34,779
In a full-scale power plant with an organic moderator reactor, this exchanger will be replaced by steam generators to harness the 16,000 thermal kilowatts produced by the reactor.

43
00:05:39,959 --> 00:05:50,039
A significant advantage of using an organic substance as a coolant is that it does not produce appreciable corrosive effects on ordinary structural materials.

44
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:59,660
The Ombre Core Tank was constructed with low-alloy steel, and all thermal stresses were completely

45
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:04,100
relieved in a suitable furnace.

46
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:13,800
The specifications included a pressure of 28 kg per cm2, a temperature of 177 °C,

47
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:19,759
and a material working coefficient of 1,000 kg per cm2.

48
00:06:19,759 --> 00:06:24,860
The tank underwent fuel inspections as soon as it was removed from the furnace.

49
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:29,599
The specifications for the top section of the tank were the same.

50
00:06:29,599 --> 00:06:37,279
Once machined and received, the vessel was dispatched to the OMBRE site for installation.

51
00:06:37,279 --> 00:06:43,879
A 60-cycle induction heating system was installed on all tanks and pipelines of OMBRE so that

52
00:06:43,879 --> 00:06:48,800
the system's temperature would be above the hydrocarbon's melting point before the

53
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:51,420
reactor begin operating.

54
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:57,600
The tank housed in the core is approximately 8.5 meters tall with an internal diameter

55
00:06:57,600 --> 00:07:04,540
of 1.35 meters and a wall thickness of 2.54 centimeters.

56
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:10,680
The cavity where the tank is located is lined with corrugated galvanized steel plates.

57
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:16,780
The tank was placed on a concrete slab supported by a rock base and galleries were arranged

58
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:20,060
for the main cooling ducts.

59
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:25,700
After installing the core, the pipes were connected to the galleries, and these were filled.

60
00:07:25,700 --> 00:07:30,500
For OMRE, plate-type fuel elements were adopted.

61
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:36,260
To manufacture each fuel plate, a mixture of the stainless steel and uranium oxide powder

62
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:40,580
was prepared, with 25% of the mixture's weight

63
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:41,780
being uranium oxide.

64
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:56,140
The mixture was subjected to a pressure of 6,300 kilograms per centimeter squared.

65
00:07:56,139 --> 00:08:19,300
The assembly was hardened by heat treatment and encased in a stainless steel cladding.

66
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:24,579
During this stage of manufacturing, the fuel element plates were referred to as sandwiches.

67
00:08:27,379 --> 00:08:33,700
In a controlled atmosphere furnace, the sandwich preparations were located before being hot rolled.

68
00:08:39,379 --> 00:08:42,820
The final thickness was achieved through cold rolling.

69
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:52,460
After cutting and machining the plates to the required dimensions, the assembly of the

70
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:58,000
fuel elements begin.

71
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:05,780
Each onward fuel element contains 16 active fuel plates.

72
00:09:05,779 --> 00:09:15,860
The plates were adequately spaced to allow for coolant circulation.

73
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:22,159
With the side edges and seams welded to form a rectangular box, the fuel element approached

74
00:09:22,159 --> 00:09:25,779
the final form.

75
00:09:25,779 --> 00:09:30,919
Stainless steel boxes were attached to the ends to secure the fuel element to the upper

76
00:09:30,919 --> 00:09:33,980
and lower grid plates.

77
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:40,100
An inert model was placed in the core assembly to check dimensions and fit.

78
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:49,960
A locking device keeps the element in position in the core.

79
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:55,600
The grid plate has 36 spaces for field elements.

80
00:09:55,600 --> 00:10:02,120
The OMRI Neutron Source consists of an antimony oxide capsule connected to an extension and

81
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:09,960
inserted into a beryllium tube. A space was reserved in the grid plate mesh for

82
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:19,500
the neutron source. Control rods which also serve as safety rods were assembled

83
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:25,179
in pairs. 12 guide holes for the control rods were symmetrically arranged between

84
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:36,180
the spaces for the fuel elements. It was necessary to separate the upper grip

85
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:41,020
plate from the thermal shield before installing this structure into the core

86
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:48,760
tank. After placing the grip plate in control rod structures in the core tank,

87
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:55,000
their assembly begin. The rod damper cylinders were attached to a suitable

88
00:10:55,000 --> 00:11:04,279
bridge then inserted into the core tank. The six control locking devices were then connected

89
00:11:04,279 --> 00:11:11,639
and the rods were attached. The damper cylinder bridge was lowered into its proper position.

90
00:11:14,519 --> 00:11:19,159
A rack and pinion system is used to move the rods during reactor operation

91
00:11:19,159 --> 00:11:24,860
and the spring trigger system is used for rapid insurgent and emergencies.

92
00:11:26,039 --> 00:11:31,519
Each locking device is connected to a piston that cushions the fall in the cylinders.

93
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:39,039
Once installed, the rods were tested for abrupt and complete shutdown scenarios.

94
00:11:40,959 --> 00:11:45,860
During construction, preliminary tests were conducted on all reactor components,

95
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:51,860
components, circuits, and other systems to ensure OMBRE was built according to project

96
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:55,720
specifications.

97
00:11:55,720 --> 00:12:01,000
The OMBRE facilities were then handed over to the operating personnel for the remaining

98
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:08,560
tests.

99
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:13,399
The tests and verifications that followed involved special and detailed processes of

100
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:21,620
reactor operation. All systems were checked including induction and

101
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:28,500
resistance heating circuits, inner gas cover and purge systems, radiation

102
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:38,199
detection equipment, heat exchangers and blowers, fire detectors, alarm systems,

103
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:55,000
auxiliary cooling systems, remote valve controls, ventilation systems, and all associated instruments.

104
00:12:55,000 --> 00:13:04,900
Kerosene was used to test the piping network and samples taken from internal filters indicated the system's purity.

105
00:13:04,899 --> 00:13:16,899
After verifying the auxiliary power and heating circuits, the melting tank was filled with the adopted organic fluid.

106
00:13:16,899 --> 00:13:32,899
The final tests for loading and unloading fuel elements were conducted with the normal volume of organic fluid in the reactor assembly.

107
00:13:32,899 --> 00:13:42,399
When critical mass loading began, the control rod drive mechanisms were placed on a special assembly platform.

108
00:13:42,399 --> 00:13:53,899
Specialized detection devices were used and the reactor was prepared for the initial electron source.

109
00:13:53,899 --> 00:14:08,199
After obtaining the necessary reports to guarantee the reactor's safe operation, the core loading was completed.

110
00:14:08,199 --> 00:14:15,740
The next phase of testing involved calibrating the nuclear system and operating at low power.

111
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:29,740
The system was pressurized with nitrogen, the primary cooling pumps were started, and power levels were gradually increased until the cooling flow reached normal levels.

112
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:35,740
The operational characteristics of the reactor were determined at various power levels.

113
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:49,580
Once the low-power operation tests were successfully completed, OMBRE became a large-scale testing laboratory, being the first to use a hydrocarbon as a moderator, reflector, and coolant.

114
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:54,720
This reactor provides essential data for solving energy production challenges.
